    'schemas/assertion.xml': '<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>\n<!--\n  socom assertion — a machine-verifiable, replayable claim captured from a\n  closed session. One row per <command> in a handoff\'s <evidence> block:\n  a VERIFY command plus its EXPECTed exit code. This is the SOCOM-native form\n  of Akili\'s extract-assertions.sh (ASSERT | VERIFY | EXPECT | CATEGORY) — but\n  the source is the handoff we already write, not a separate markdown journal,\n  and there is NO model in the loop (the only one of Akili\'s five extractors\n  that is purely deterministic; the rest are deferred to preserve the L0 floor).\n\n  WHY — verify-never-claim made durable: "Evidence is replayable, not quotable:\n  record the command and exit code." A handoff\'s evidence is prose-adjacent and\n  dies with the session; an assertion row is a re-runnable check that outlives it.\n  `socom introspect` harvests them at closeout; a future seat can replay the log\n  to confirm the inherited state still holds (the next-session drift scan, made\n  executable rather than asserted).\n\n  STORAGE — append-only JSONL at .socom/assertions/log.jsonl (one JSON object\n  per line, keys exactly the <field> names below), for the same reason as the\n  ledger (schemas/ledger.xml): high-volume, automation-written, a flat `>>`\n  append is race-light where rewriting an XML close-tag is not. Append-only and\n  in-repo (§git-is-source-of-truth): a row, once written, is never edited.\n  IDEMPOTENT — the `id` (source_handoff + index) is the dedup key: re-running\n  introspect on the same handoff appends nothing.\n\n  BRIDGE — an assertion whose command failed UNEXPECTEDLY (expect_exit != 0 with\n  no explanatory note) is a captured one-off failure; introspect births a\n  PROVISIONAL lesson candidate from it (source="introspect"), a second birth path\n  alongside the cycle->lesson hotspot bridge. Provisional, not active: a one-off\n  earns active only by re-confirmation (schemas/lesson.xml lifecycle). A no