    'schemas/lesson.xml': '<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>\n<!--\n  socom lesson — a durable, retrievable rule earned from experience. The\n  engine SOCOM only gestured at (the .socom/lessons/ stub). Ported from\n  Akili\'s lesson system (LESSON-SYSTEM-ENGINEERING.md): a lesson is BORN\n  provisional, EARNS active by re-confirmation, and is RETIRED (never\n  deleted) when falsified — status indicates disposition, history is kept.\n\n  The dominant birth path is the eval->lesson bridge: `socom cycle` surfaces\n  hotspots (promises with repeated `broken` verdicts); `socom lesson\n  candidates` turns each into a provisional lesson citing the cycle it came\n  from. A lesson consumes the cycle\'s PUBLISHED hotspots (published-language),\n  never the ledger internals.\n\n  RETRIEVAL is free: this artifact lives at .socom/lessons/<id>.xml, so\n  `socom index` (which rglobs .socom/**.xml) emits its embed="true" elements\n  as chunks, filterable by the `domain` attribute. The lifecycle filter\n  excludes state="retired" from retrieval — a retired lesson stays on disk\n  and queryable for audit, but never surfaces as live guidance.\n\n  LIFECYCLE attribute drives the deterministic retrieval map; state drives\n  the live/retired filter; source records provenance (cycle|human|council).\n-->\n<lesson id="L-P-2026-0612-002"\n        domain="data-pipeline"\n        state="provisional"\n        source="cycle"\n        lifecycle="mid-session">\n\n  <!-- WHAT — the rule/guard, the embedded chunk that earns retrieval. -->\n  <statement embed="true">\n    A failed product run must record status=\'failure\' in dbo.run BEFORE the\n    notebook re-raises — assert the insert is in the except path on every\n    change to a run-recording promise.\n  </statement>\n\n  <!-- WHY — the reasoning, so the rule is applied with judgment not by rote. -->\n  <why embed="true">\n    The promise P-2026-0612-002 broke twice on the same contract: the failure\n    path skipped run-recording, so the 